    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256">

                <pb facs="0648" n="534" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg534"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/8–343</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Campbell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Adviser on Political Relations</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dunn</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-03">August 3rd,
                        1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Jimmy</hi>, I enclose a copy of a telegram
                    from the Foreign Office on the subject of an approach made to our Ambassador at
                        Lisbon.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d256-f1"/> Although the peace feeler described
                    in this telegram has been overtaken by events, the Foreign Office thought that
                    you would be interested to have an account of it.</p>
                <p>I also enclose a copy of a telegram received from the Ambassador in Ankara
                    recording approaches made by the Italian Ambassador there to the Turkish
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs. You may have received a report of this from Ankara
                    through your own channels,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d256-f2"/> but if not you may
                    find it interesting to have this telegram.</p>
                <p>Yours ever,</p>
                <closer>(for <signed>Sir R. Campbell</signed>) <lb/>
                    <signed>W G <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hayter</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d256-a1.xml" xpointer="d256-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d256-a2.xml" xpointer="d256-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
